# VM Operations

## Environment

- **VM IP**: 192.168.8.65, user: `x`
- **OS**: Artix Linux, init: dinit (not systemd — use `dinitctl`, not `systemctl`)
- **Project path**: `/home/x/dev/model-archival/model-archival/`
- **Screen session**: `archiver` (`screen -S archiver bash run.sh --all`). **`deploy/setup-artix.sh`** / **`deploy/setup-mxlinux.sh`** also install **tmux**, **powerline** (`python-powerline` / `python3-powerline`), **powerline-fonts** (`fonts-powerline` on Debian), clone **tmux-powerline** to `~/.tmux-powerline` (configure `~/.tmux.conf` per [erikw/tmux-powerline](https://github.com/erikw/tmux-powerline)), **fish**, and **Oh My Fish** (non-interactive; skip with `OMF_SKIP=1`).

## Disk layout

| Label | Device | Mount | Size | Role |
|-------|--------|-------|------|------|
| D1 | /dev/sdc | /mnt/models/d1 | 5.5 TB | Large models + `.tmp/` scratch |
| D2 | /dev/sdd | /mnt/models/d2 | 2.7 TB | Mid-size models + Tier D |
| D3 | /dev/sde | /mnt/models/d3 | 2.7 TB | GGUF quants + archiver infra (logs, state, archive/) |
| D5 | /dev/sdb | /mnt/models/d5 | 916 GB | Completed models only when `drive: d5` in registry |

In-progress downloads land in `D1/.tmp/` (then `D3/.tmp` if needed) — never on D5 or root SSD.

**Download size cap (default):** `run.sh` passes **`--max-model-download-gib 80`** (binary GiB, summed HF file sizes). Checkpoints above that are marked **`deferred_large`** in `run_state.json` and are not retried until state is cleared or you use **`--no-max-model-download`** / a higher limit for a dedicated run.

**Ollama cache sync** (`model-archival/scripts/ollama-sync.sh`): default destination is **`/mnt/models/d5/supermicro`**. If **D5 is full**, continue syncs on **D2** with **`ARCHIVAL_VM_DEST=/mnt/models/d2/supermicro`** (create the directory first). Sync is additive-only; existing trees under `d5/supermicro` stay until you move or delete them.

**Live Ollama + vLLM HF cache on D5:** Prefer **`OLLAMA_HOME=/mnt/models/d5/ollama`** and **`VLLM_ARCHIVE_ROOT=/mnt/models/d5/vllm`** (`ollama-hosting/config/env-archive-vm.sh`, `vllm-hosting/config/env-archive-vm-vllm.sh`). To merge older **`d2/ollama`**, **`d1/vllm`**, etc. onto D5, run **`deploy/consolidate-ollama-vllm-caches-to-d5.sh`** on the VM (dry-run first). **D5 ~916 GiB** — confirm **`du -sh`** totals fit before applying.

## Before rebooting — always stop gracefully

```bash
bash /home/x/dev/model-archival/model-archival/stop.sh   # wait for "stopped cleanly"
# then reboot — skipping this can corrupt D1/D2 (requires fsck to fix)
```

## If drives not mounted after reboot

```bash
sudo bash /home/x/dev/model-archival/model-archival/deploy/vm-mount-disks.sh
```

## If a drive shows "Structure needs cleaning"

```bash
sudo fsck.ext4 -y /dev/sdXN   # fix filesystem
sudo mount /mnt/models/dN     # then remount
```

## VPN (Surfshark via OpenVPN)

```bash
# Status check
surfshark-vpn status 2>/dev/null; curl -s https://ipinfo.io | grep -E '"ip"|"org"'
# Should show: "AS9009 M247 Europe SRL" — not your ISP

# Connect (if not auto-started by dinit)
sudo openvpn --config /etc/openvpn/client/surfshark/nl-ams.prod.surfshark.com_udp.ovpn \
             --auth-user-pass /etc/openvpn/client/surfshark.auth \
             --daemon --log /var/log/surfshark-openvpn.log

# Auto-starts via dinit: /etc/dinit.d/boot.d/openvpn-surfshark (service: openvpn-surfshark)
# If bandwidth is poor, try another EU server: de-fra, uk-lon, fr-par (configs in /etc/openvpn/client/surfshark/).
```

Note: Surfshark AUR CLI (`surfshark-vpn` binary) is broken — use OpenVPN + openvpn-surfshark service.
Note: Surfshark flatpak GUI fails with "No internet connection" on connman systems — use OpenVPN.

## Monitor downloads

```bash
screen -S archiver -X hardcopy /tmp/s.txt && cat /tmp/s.txt   # snapshot screen
watch -n 30 cat /mnt/models/d3/STATUS.md                       # live status file
```
